.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt FIDLGEN-BSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fidlgen-bsd
.Nd generate native C and C++ FIDL bindings
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -json Ar file
.Fl -root Ar directory
.Op Fl -c
.Op Fl -dependency-json Ar file
.Op Fl -templates Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility consumes the JSON intermediate representation produced by
.Cm fidlc
and generates native 5BSD client, server, event, and natural type bindings.
The
.Fl -c
option also emits a C header and a C++ implementation of its C ABI.
Use
.Fl -dependency-json
once per dependency-library JSON file, including transitive dependencies.
The adapter orders and generates the complete supplied graph.
Missing libraries, duplicate inputs, cycles, and inconsistent available
imported-declaration metadata are rejected.
The native
.Li zx.Handle
mapping needs no separate Zircon runtime library.
Unsupported schemas fail generation without replacing previous outputs.
.Pp
Generated code uses
.Xr libfidl_bsd 3
and native capability-channel descriptors.
No Fuchsia dispatcher or Zircon syscall emulation is required.
The natural C++ types are produced by upstream's fidlgen_cpp templates,
run by the adapter's own template engine; the installed adapter uses its
private copy of the generator and templates under
.Pa /usr/libexec/fidl .
The
.Fl -templates
option names another template directory and is for toolchain development.
.Pp
The host tools require Python 3.12.
.Cm fidl-lint
also needs the RE2 library from ports.
The generated binaries do not need Python.
buildworld generates the system's own bindings the same way, with a
build-only
.Cm fidlc
and Python; see
.Xr build 7 .
This SDK remains experimental; its presence does not mean system providers
have migrated to FIDL.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate C and C++ bindings for a local schema:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fidlc --json example.json --files example.fidl
fidlgen-bsd --json example.json --root generated --c
pkgconf --cflags --libs fidl
.Ed
.Pp
Compile generated natural types and the C bridge as C++20.
Compile a C application as C11 and link its objects with the generated
objects and the libraries returned by pkgconf.
Add
.Fl -static
to the pkgconf command to obtain private library dependencies for static
runtime linking.
The generated public C header is usable by a C compiler.
For several libraries, compile each library's emitted
.Pa cpp/natural_types.cc ,
.Pa cpp/common_types.cc ,
and
.Pa c/bsd.cc
exactly once.
The generated
.Pa c/bridge.h
is private C++ conversion support shared between dependent bindings;
C application sources include
.Pa c/bsd.h .
.Pp
Generate a service and its common type library:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
fidlc --json common.json --files common.fidl
fidlc --json service.json --files common.fidl --files service.fidl
fidlgen-bsd --json service.json --dependency-json common.json \
    --root generated --c
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libfidl_bsd 3 ,
.Xr build 7 ,
.Xr fidl 7
